# Native service definitions (data, never a shell script).
# Format: executable [argv ...] [respawn[=N]]
# A bare respawn permits three restarts; N is bounded to 0..16.
#
# A file with no service records (this one) does not exit daemond: the
# supervisor stays resident, keeps PID 1 alive, and serves daemonctl on the
# control socket until SIGTERM/SIGINT.  A missing /etc/rc is treated the same
# way and reported with its errno.  Once at least one service is configured,
# daemond exits cleanly after every configured service has exited and no
# restart is pending.
